#!/bin/sh
# Re-register AirPlay (shairport-sync) mDNS whenever the Wi-Fi STA (re)associates.
#
# THE BUG (diagnosed 2026-09-09, copper vs silver on the same AP):
# At boot every service starts in parallel, and the ath9k STA associates a few
# seconds in WITH a brief association wobble (a boot-only Reason-6 re-assoc; the
# wwan IPv4 address is withdrawn then re-added — visible in the avahi log as
# "Withdrawing address record ... New relevant interface ... Registering new
# address record"). shairport-sync registers its _raop._tcp service with avahi
# over D-Bus at startup; if that registration lands DURING the address flap, the
# Avahi entry group is dropped and nothing re-establishes it once the link is
# stable. Result: the device is fully up (RTSP :5000 listening, engine running)
# but INVISIBLE to every AirPlay controller until shairport-sync is restarted.
# It's a race, so it bites intermittently — a device can be silently un-airplayable
# with everything otherwise "green". See memory: airplay-mdns-boot-race.
#
# THE FIX:
# hotplug.d/iface fires on netifd's ifup for the logical STA interface (wwan) —
# which happens at the final boot association AND at the wobble (an L3 address
# re-add), exactly when we need to re-announce. netcheck's ~20s poll can't see the
# sub-second reassoc; this hook does. A full ifup only occurs on a real
# (re)association (which already dropped any active stream), so bouncing shairport
# here does not interrupt normal playback. shairport-sync's procd init makes the
# restart idempotent even if this races its own boot start.
#
# No-op on variants without shairport (e.g. the LMS build) and when it's disabled.
# NOTE: hotplug.d scripts are SOURCED, so never `exit` here (it would abort the
# whole hotplug chain) — guard with a positive if-block instead.
if [ "$ACTION" = ifup ] && [ "$INTERFACE" = wwan ] \
   && [ -x /etc/init.d/shairport-sync ] && /etc/init.d/shairport-sync enabled 2>/dev/null; then
	logger -t beep-airplay "wwan ifup -> restarting shairport-sync to (re)register _raop mDNS"
	/etc/init.d/shairport-sync restart 2>/dev/null
fi
